PR #42 introduces a custom-provider regression: `cite` accepts `././sample.txt`, but `affected({changed:['././sample.txt']})` silently skips that citation using the identical operand. The report says `complete: true` and `sourceComplete: true` without reading the changed source. The same built-package reproduction returns the affected row immediately before #42.

Verified on `049dc82bdb0edfa259ffd6c8454cd9104d4b3f29` and its parent `2c538630acd8be8d24a0c2537daf400f1ffef717`, with Node 24.19.0 and lockfile dependencies. The adapter is a deterministic in-process fixture; no source file, service, or model is involved.

### Exact source

- [Custom-provider normalization removes exactly one leading `./`, so it is not idempotent](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-evidence/blob/049dc82bdb0edfa259ffd6c8454cd9104d4b3f29/src/sources.ts#L8-L17).
- [Citation creation stores the result of one normalization](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-evidence/blob/049dc82bdb0edfa259ffd6c8454cd9104d4b3f29/src/evidence.ts#L11-L19).
- [The new filter normalizes both the raw operand and the already-normalized stored source](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-evidence/blob/049dc82bdb0edfa259ffd6c8454cd9104d4b3f29/src/evidence.ts#L105-L117).

For this input, the stored source is `./sample.txt`. At filtering time, the raw operand becomes `./sample.txt`, while the stored source becomes `sample.txt`. They cannot match, so the source is skipped before verification.

### Reproduction

```sh
review=$(mktemp -d)
git clone --quiet https://github.com/unbraind/pm-evidence.git "$review/package"
cd "$review/package"
git checkout --quiet 049dc82bdb0edfa259ffd6c8454cd9104d4b3f29
npm ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund
npm run build
cat > repro-custom-path.mjs <<'JS'
import { mkdtemp } from 'node:fs/promises';
import {tmpdir} from 'node:os';
import {join} from 'node:path';
import {PmClient} from '@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk';
import {cite,check,affected} from './dist/index.js';
import {digest} from './dist/src/core.js';
const root=await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(),'evidence-repro-'));const workspace=join(root,'tracker');
const client=new PmClient({cwd:root,pmRoot:workspace,author:'fixture',noExtensions:true});
await client.init('sample',{defaults:true,agentGuidance:'skip',mergeFence:false});
const item=(await client.create({title:'Opaque source',type:'Task'})).item.id;
let changed=false;const calls=[];const adapters=[{provider:'opaque',read:async source=>{calls.push(source);const text=source+(changed?':new':':old');return{text,revision:digest(text)};}}];
const opts={workspace,root,author:'fixture',adapters,budget:10000};
await cite(item,'././sample.txt',{...opts,provider:'opaque',selector:{kind:'lines',start:1,end:1}});
changed=true;
const all=await check([],{...opts,record:false});
const filtered=await affected({...opts,changed:['././sample.txt']});
console.log(JSON.stringify({check_rows:all.rows.length,check_freshness:all.rows[0]?.freshness,filtered_rows:filtered.rows.length,source_complete:filtered.receipt.sourceComplete,complete:filtered.receipt.complete,filtered_reads:filtered.receipt.verification.sourceReads,calls}));
JS
PM_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1 PM_AGENT_PROBES=0 NODE_ENV=test node repro-custom-path.mjs
```

Observed on #42:

```json
{"check_rows":1,"check_freshness":"changed","filtered_rows":0,"source_complete":true,"complete":true,"filtered_reads":0,"calls":["sample.txt","sample.txt"]}
```

Run the exact same fixture against the parent:

```sh
git checkout --quiet 2c538630acd8be8d24a0c2537daf400f1ffef717
npm run build
PM_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1 PM_AGENT_PROBES=0 NODE_ENV=test node repro-custom-path.mjs
```

Observed before #42:

```json
{"check_rows":1,"check_freshness":"changed","filtered_rows":1,"source_complete":true,"complete":true,"filtered_reads":1,"calls":["sample.txt","sample.txt","sample.txt"]}
```

### Expected versus actual

Expected: a filter using the identical accepted source operand finds the changed citation. Alternatively, unsupported identities must refuse explicitly before citation creation; an accepted source must not disappear behind an affirmative completeness receipt.

Actual: the unfiltered check reports the citation as changed, but filtered impact analysis returns zero rows, performs zero source reads, and reports complete/source-complete success. This worked before the merged normalization change.

### Impact and suggested direction

Changed-source-driven review can miss custom-provider evidence and its dependent tasks after the upgrade. The new filesystem normalization tests pass, including the custom-provider repeated-separator case; they do not cover repeated leading `./` with the same creation/filter operand.

Make provider identity handling consistent across raw operands, stored descriptors and adapter/cache reads. Either use an idempotent provider-specific canonicalization or distinguish raw and already-normalized identities so a stored custom identity is not stripped again. Preserve opaque custom identifiers and legacy citations rather than applying filesystem normalization indiscriminately. Add a before/after regression for this exact-input property.

Duplicate check: all-state searches for `custom provider path`, `canonical affected`, `opaque`, and `custom normalization`, plus the full issue inventory. Closed [#40](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-evidence/issues/40) concerns equivalent **filesystem** spellings and explicitly asks to preserve arbitrary custom-provider identities. This report is the newly introduced **custom-provider** regression in its fix; the parent control succeeds. No duplicate of #40 is being asserted for the fixed filesystem case.
